XLIO Testing Environment
=======================

This set of tests is based on Google Test C++ environment 
https://github.com/google/googletest

Testing XLIO Extended API
------------------------
1. Enable EXTRA_API_ENABLED in tests/gtest/core/xlio_base.cc
2. Compile the gtests by issuing from root directory:
   make -C tests/gtest
3. Launch tests by issuing:
   LD_PRELOAD=<path>/libxlio.so tests/gtest/gtest --addr=client_ip,server_ip

Testing Environment
-------------------
The XLIO Extended API gtest environment requires that there be two interfaces
connected back to back or via a switch. One is the server and the other is the
client.

Running the runner
------------------------------
The 'run' script allows running the tests with various XLIO configurations. 
Each profile selects a set of the tests to run and the XLIO configuration file
to use when running these tests. For each selected profile, the 'gtest' 
executable is run exactly once, with the results written to a separate directory.

After building XLIO and the gtest executable, run from the source root:

   tests/gtest/run --addr=client_ip,server_ip

This defaults to --profiles=r2c-full,wtbp . Use --help to see the available profiles.

--profiles accepts a comma-separated list of profile names.

List every profile's config and filter without addresses or a build:

   tests/gtest/run --list-profiles

Profiles use JSON template files in config/ for XLIO runtime settings. 
Every file is translated to a file written to the profile run directory, 
substituting special fields marked by @xxx@. JSON string
values (including nested objects and arrays) can use @CLIENT_IP@, @SERVER_IP@,
@PROFILE@, @RUN_DIR@, and @SOURCE_ROOT@. Addresses are those selected for the
profile, including IPv6 or loopback when applicable. Unknown placeholders fail 
before any tests run. Templates are validated in --dry-run too, without writing files. 

Select profiles explicitly, or inspect the gtest commands without executing them:

   tests/gtest/run --profiles=wtbp --addr=client_ip,server_ip
   tests/gtest/run --dry-run --addr=client_ip,server_ip

The Python 3 runner accepts both --option=value and --option value:

   tests/gtest/run --addr client_ip,server_ip --profiles r2c-full,wtbp

Override the profile's filter for every selected run with --filter:

   tests/gtest/run --addr client_ip,server_ip --filter 'tcp_sockopt.*'
   tests/gtest/run --addr=client_ip,server_ip --filter='-tcp_sockopt.*'

Use the = form when a filter starts with a dash. Without --filter, each
profile uses its CI filter. An override leaves its configuration and mode intact.

For out-of-tree builds or an installed library, supply absolute or
current-directory-relative paths:

   tests/gtest/run --addr=client_ip,server_ip \
       --gtest-bin=/build/tests/gtest/gtest \
       --xlio-lib=/install/lib/libxlio.so --output-dir=/tmp/gtest-results

Additional gtest arguments follow --, for example -- --port=55556. Use the
runner's --filter to override filters; addresses and XML output are owned by
the runner. --timeout=20m is the per-invocation default; --timeout=0 disables
it. See --help for all profiles.

Each invocation creates a unique UTC timestamped directory under --output-dir
(default ./gtest-results), for example 20261108-123456.123456Z-a1b2c3d4.

--dry-run creates no directories or files. 

The summary reports passed, failed, runtime-skipped, and disabled tests
separately. DISABLED_ tests are excluded unless --gtest_also_run_disabled_tests
is passed after --; GTEST_SKIP() stops a selected test at runtime.

LD_PRELOAD points to the selected library, including for test subprocesses. 
The caller's environment is unchanged. The runner defaults WORKSPACE to the 
source tree only when it is not set, preserving any caller-provided value. 
Other environment variables are inherited without assigning defaults

Hardware-free runner contract checks:

   python3 tests/gtest/test_run.py


Profiles are independent of address family. Pass IPv4 or IPv6 endpoints using
--addr. CI uses r2c-full for IPv4 and r2c-default for IPv6. Additional gtest
arguments can follow --, for example:

   tests/gtest/run --profiles r2c-default --addr 2001:db8::1,2001:db8::2 -- -r fdff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff:ffff
